---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — dord.racing"
  description="Privacy policy for dord.racing: newsletter email, your chosen country, visit counting without cookies (Cloudflare Web Analytics) and affiliate links (Travelpayouts)."
  canonicalUrl="https://dord.racing/legal/privacy"
>
  <header>
    <div class="header--left">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <div class="meta">LEGAL · DORD.RACING</div>
      <Nav activePage="calendar" />
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="main-content" class="legal-page">
    <a href={`${base}/`} class="back-link">← Back to Calendar</a>

    <div class="legal-body">

      <p class="legal-date">Last updated: November 13, 2026 — Google Analytics removed; visits are now counted with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which sets no cookies and stores nothing on your device (sections 5, 7 and 8)</p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>dord.racing is operated by Yann Durandet, based in France. For privacy-related questions, contact us at <a class="js-mailto" data-u="durandet.yann.pro" data-d="gmail.com" data-show></a>. As the site is operated from France, it is subject to the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).</p>

      <h2>2. Data we collect</h2>
      <p>dord.racing has no account system and no contact form. The only personal data we hold ourselves is the email address of people who subscribe to our newsletter (section 4). Beyond that, we do not collect, store, or process personal data about you directly.</p>
      <p>Your calendar filter preferences (series, region, and category selections) are saved to your browser's <strong>local storage</strong> under the key <code>motorsportFilters</code>. Local storage is a browser-side mechanism — this data is stored only on your device, is never transmitted to any server, and is not accessible to us. You can clear it at any time by clearing your browser's site data for dord.racing.</p>
      <p>The same applies to the country you choose for broadcaster listings, saved under the key <code>dord-country</code> (see section 3).</p>

      <h2>3. Your country (where to watch)</h2>
      <p>TV channels and streaming services differ from one country to another. So that the watch page and the "How to watch" block on each series page show the ones that work where you are, the watch page asks you where you are watching from the first time you open it. We use your answer for that and nothing else.</p>
      <p>You can answer in three ways:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Use my location.</strong> Your browser asks dord.racing's own <code>/api/country</code> endpoint, which replies with a two-letter country code. That code is the one Cloudflare works out from your IP address, the same lookup it performs for every request it serves (see section 8). We do not use your browser's location feature (GPS or Wi-Fi), so we never receive coordinates. The site's code does not read, log or store your IP address, and does not store or share the country code it returns.</li>
        <li><strong>Choose your country</strong> from the list. Nothing is detected, and nothing is sent anywhere.</li>
        <li><strong>No thanks.</strong> We then show the broadcasters for the USA by default, which may not be available in your region.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Your answer is saved in your browser's <strong>local storage</strong> under the key <code>dord-country</code>. It is a country code, the word <code>global</code> if you choose "Another country (worldwide options)", or the word <code>default</code> if you answer "No thanks". It stays on your device, is never transmitted to any server, and is used only to choose which broadcasters to display. You can change it at any time with the "Change country" button on the watch and series pages, or clear it by clearing your browser's site data for dord.racing. Closing the popup without answering saves nothing, so you will be asked again on your next visit.</p>

      <h2>4. Newsletter (From The Pit Wall)</h2>
      <p>If you subscribe to our weekly newsletter, we store your <strong>email address</strong>, the date you subscribed and whether your subscription is awaiting confirmation, active or unsubscribed. We collect nothing else about you through the sign-up: no name, and no other details.</p>
      <p>This data is kept in a database hosted by Turso, and the emails (one when you sign up, then one each week) are delivered by Resend, an email delivery service. Resend processes your address to send the emails and may record delivery status such as delivered or bounced. Some of these providers are based outside the EU and may process data outside the European Economic Area; see <a href="https://turso.tech/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Turso's</a> and <a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Resend's</a> privacy policies. We use your address only to send you the newsletter, and we do not sell or share it with anyone else.</p>
      <p>Every email has an unsubscribe link, or you can reply with "unsubscribe" in the subject line. Unsubscribing stops the emails and keeps your address on file, flagged as unsubscribed, so that we do not email you again. To have it deleted, write to us at the address in section 12.</p>

      <h2>5. Analytics and the cookie banner</h2>
      <p>We count visits with Cloudflare Web Analytics, described in section 8. It sets no cookies and stores nothing on your device, so it does not depend on the cookie banner.</p>
      <p>Until November 2026 this site also used Google Analytics 4, loaded only with consent. It has been removed: no Google Analytics script is loaded any more, and any <code>_ga</code> cookies it set on your device are deleted the next time you open a page here.</p>
      <p>The cookie consent banner shown on your first visit now covers one thing: the Travelpayouts affiliate script (section 6). Your choice is stored in a <code>cookie_consent</code> cookie (1-year expiry) so the banner does not reappear on subsequent visits. You can change your choice at any time with <strong>Cookie settings</strong> at the bottom of the page.</p>

      <h2 id="affiliates">6. Affiliate links and third-party cookies</h2>
      <p>With your consent, dord.racing loads a script from <strong>Travelpayouts</strong>, the affiliate network we work with, served from <code>tp-em.com</code>. It lets Travelpayouts recognise links on our pages that lead to its travel partners and turn them into affiliate links, and record clicks on those links so that bookings can be credited to us.</p>
      <p>The script is only loaded after you click <strong>Accept</strong> in the cookie consent banner. If you click Decline, it is never loaded and Travelpayouts receives nothing from your visit to dord.racing. The same <code>cookie_consent</code> cookie records your choice, and you can withdraw consent the same way, with <strong>Cookie settings</strong> at the bottom of any page: the script is then no longer loaded from the next page on.</p>
      <p>When the script loads, your browser connects to Travelpayouts' servers, which receive the technical data any web request carries: your IP address, browser type, and the address of the page you are viewing. The script may set or read cookies or similar identifiers on your device to attribute clicks and bookings. We do not send Travelpayouts your email address or any other personal data, and we do not receive personal data back from it, only aggregated click and booking reports. This processing is governed by <a href="https://www.travelpayouts.com/en/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Travelpayouts' privacy policy</a>, and Travelpayouts may process data outside the European Economic Area. The site works the same whether you accept or decline.</p>
      <p>Some links on this site are affiliate links. When you click an affiliate link, you are redirected to a third-party platform (such as a hotel, tour, or travel booking partner). These platforms may set their own cookies on your device in order to track referrals and attribute bookings to us.</p>
      <p>These cookies are set by third parties, not by dord.racing. We have no control over them. The data collected by affiliate platforms is governed by their own privacy policies. We encourage you to review those policies before making a purchase.</p>
      <p>Affiliate cookies typically persist for 7 to 30 days depending on the programme. They are used solely to determine whether a purchase resulted from a click on our site, so that we can receive the applicable commission.</p>

      <h2>7. Legal basis for processing (GDPR)</h2>
      <p>Your newsletter subscription (section 4) rests on your consent (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a)), which you give by submitting your address and can withdraw at any time by unsubscribing.</p>
      <p>The Travelpayouts script (section 6) is loaded only on the basis of your explicit consent (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a)). Affiliate tracking cookies set by third-party platforms when you click a link fall under the legitimate interests of those platforms (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)); their data processing is governed by their own policies.</p>
      <p>Cloudflare Web Analytics (section 8) rests on our legitimate interest in knowing how many people use the site and which pages they read (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)). It uses no cookies and no identifiers.</p>
      <p>Country detection (section 3) runs only when you click <strong>Use my location</strong>, so it rests on your own request and consent (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a)). The country you pick is a preference you set and is kept only on your device.</p>

      <h2>8. Hosting (Cloudflare)</h2>
      <p>This site runs on Cloudflare (a service of Cloudflare, Inc.), which serves its pages and runs the small server-side functions behind the newsletter sign-up and unsubscribe, the country lookup (section 3) and the weekly newsletter send. Cloudflare may collect basic server access logs (IP address, browser type, referring URL, country) as part of normal hosting and DDoS-protection operations. This is governed by <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cloudflare's Privacy Policy</a>. We do not use this data to identify individual visitors.</p>
      <p>We also use <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> to count visits. It tells us which pages are viewed, which site a visit came from, the visitor's country, browser, operating system and type of device, and how fast the page loaded. It runs on every visit and does not depend on the cookie banner, because it sets no cookies, stores nothing on your device and does not fingerprint visitors; Cloudflare states that it discards your IP address instead of storing it. What we see are totals, and we cannot identify an individual from them. Cloudflare describes the data involved in its <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/speed/observatory/rum-beacon/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">documentation</a>.</p>

      <h2>9. Fonts</h2>
      <p>Fonts (Orbitron, JetBrains Mono, Inter) are self-hosted on dord.racing. No request is made to Google Fonts or any third-party font CDN, so no IP address or browser data is transmitted to Google as a result of loading this site's typography.</p>

      <h2>10. Your rights (GDPR)</h2>
      <p>If you are located in the EU or UK, you have rights under the GDPR including the right to access, rectify, or erase personal data held about you, and to object to or restrict its processing.</p>
      <p>The only personal data dord.racing holds itself is the email address of newsletter subscribers (section 4). Write to us at the address in section 12 and we will tell you what we hold about you and delete it on request. Unsubscribing stops the emails but keeps your address on file, flagged as unsubscribed, until you ask us to delete it. For data held by the third-party services named in this policy (Google, Cloudflare, Resend, Turso, Travelpayouts and affiliate partners), you can also contact those services directly.</p>
      <p>To withdraw analytics and affiliate consent, open <strong>Cookie settings</strong> at the bottom of any page and choose Decline. To stop newsletter emails, use the unsubscribe link in any of them. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with your data protection authority; in France this is the CNIL (<a href="https://www.cnil.fr" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cnil.fr</a>).</p>

      <h2>11. Changes</h2>
      <p>This policy may be updated as we add new features. Material changes will be reflected in the "Last updated" date above.</p>

      <h2>12. Contact</h2>
      <p>Privacy questions: <a class="js-mailto" data-u="durandet.yann.pro" data-d="gmail.com" data-show></a></p>

    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    max-width: var(--w-prose);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1.5rem 4rem;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }
  .back-link:hover { color: var(--text-muted-2); }

  .legal-body {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    color: var(--text-muted-3);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .legal-date {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--text-meta);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .legal-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-2xs-3);
    color: var(--accent-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin: 2rem 0 0.6rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-subtle);
  }

  .legal-body p {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .legal-body ul {
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
  }

  .legal-body li {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .legal-body a {
    color: var(--link);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .legal-body a:hover { color: var(--link-hover); text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
